    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "2479e5f5_f6893886",
        "filename": "java/app_test.go",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 2449,
      "author": {
        "id": 1039338
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-05-19T11:21:12Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "You can\u0027t just globally replace android.test.mock.stubs with android.test.mock because that would change behavior in some cases. It would cause any library that does not set sdk_version to switch from using stubs to using the actual implementation code. I don\u0027t consider that a good change as it can open code up to accidentally using implementation details of a class that will cause compatibility issues in future. e.g. http://cs/android/cts/tests/tests/mimemap/Android.bp?l\u003d20 would change.\n\nEven if you could fix all the existing usages that would not be sufficient because of the framework modules that do not currently use java_sdk_library but which need to be converted to use java_sdk_library.\n\nThey reference the stubs library directly because they are currently created as standalone java_library modules and so have no other choice. Those references cannot be replaced with the name of the java_sdk_library until after the module has been converted to a java_sdk_library. The references could theoretically be updated in the same change as the conversion is done but that is not practical.\n\nIt is not practical because there are ~8 modules that need converting to java_sdk_library and references to the stubs library for those modules are used together so will be a source of conflict if they are changed in separate changes. Doing them all in one set of changes in one topic would be a nightmare.\n\nConverting them to java_sdk_library can be done separately with no conflicts. Once that conversion is done then we can change the names.\n\nCleaning up is a good thing to do but it is not a priority right now.",
      "parentUuid": "a8858b88_7c6361f8",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 2449,
        "startChar": 18,
        "endLine": 2449,
        "endChar": 28
      },
      "revId": "0facbe0cd76326d389c3e5c722577ca3f7db84f8",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "135d1c63_b5752505",
        "filename": "java/app_test.go",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 2449,
      "author": {
        "id": 1132673
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-05-19T11:43:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e switch from using stubs to using the actual implementation code\n\nI see that that is a change that was introduced with https://android-review.googlesource.com/c/platform/build/soong/+/1215335/3/java/sdk_library.go#685 \n\n\u003e it can open code up to accidentally using implementation details of a class that will cause compatibility issues in future.\n\nRight. CTS modules that don\u0027t use sdk_version is a well-known (and very old) problem. I think that should be addressed anyway. If for some reason a module has chosen to keep `platform_apis: true`, it\u0027s their choice and they should pay for the decision.\n\n\n\u003e The references could theoretically be updated in the same change as the conversion is done but that is not practical.\n\nI don\u0027t think this is a big problem, we always had multiple CLs tied together as a topic. If we really want to submit those changes separately, we could temporarily (or exceptionally) allow references to stubs library only during the transition period. In other words, I think such an exceptional and one-time use-case shouldn\u0027t be the reason for exposing stubs perhaps permanently.",
      "parentUuid": "2479e5f5_f6893886",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 2449,
        "startChar": 18,
        "endLine": 2449,
        "endChar": 28
      },
      "revId": "0facbe0cd76326d389c3e5c722577ca3f7db84f8",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1f162d83_c9347b62",
        "filename": "java/app_test.go",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 2449,
      "author": {
        "id": 1039338
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-05-19T14:08:36Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e I don\u0027t think this is a big problem, we always had multiple CLs tied together as a topic.\n\nInstead of having 8 separate changes which can be submitted separately, each of which could introduce subtle behavioral differences which are only discovered after having been submitted and require reverting (already happened) we would have 9 or 10 separate changes in separate repositories that would all need reverting if even one of them failed. Submitting them would require gaining approval from 8 different teams over and over again until all the issues are resolved.\n\nNot to mention that those repositories are all developed in different places (some in AOSP, some in rvc-dev, some in git_master) so it may not be possible to submit them all in one go under one topic due to conflicts.\n\nIt\u0027s just not practical.\n\nSeparating the functional changes from the renaming changes will greatly reduce the cost. The renaming changes will be much simpler and will be much easier to review and test if done separately.\n\n\u003e In other words, I think such an exceptional and one-time use-case shouldn\u0027t be the reason for exposing stubs perhaps permanently.\n\nOnce again, this change is not exposing stubs, they are already exposed. This change is simply testing to ensure that they work properly.\n\nIf exposing stubs is a problem (which I am not convinced it is but I\u0027ll address that in your bug) this is not making the problem worse.\n\nIf we did decide to remove all the references then cleaning up the issue isn\u0027t going to happen any time soon and this test will be easy to fix.\n\nIf you don\u0027t have any other issues with this change could you +2 it so I can make some progress and then we can move this discussion to your bug?",
      "parentUuid": "135d1c63_b5752505",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 2449,
        "startChar": 18,
        "endLine": 2449,
        "endChar": 28
